{
  "_about": "Weather and light for the maps (lane B3), one entry each. A map names its default in maps.json \"weather\"; level.set_weather(id) switches live. Sun angles in degrees (elevation above the horizon, azimuth clockwise from north). Colours are linear-ish 0-1. cloud_coverage 0 = clear, 1 = overcast; clouds draw at the quality of Settings > Graphics > Clouds. Lane B4 fields (all optional): white (tonemap white point), sun_scatter (haze lit toward the sun), height_fog_top_m and height_fog_density (fog that pools below that height), fog_sky_affect, volumetric_anisotropy, and grade {contrast, saturation, shadow_shift, highlight_shift, strength}: a film grade, shadows and highlights nudged toward a tint (scripts/world/film_grade.gd). glow_intensity and glow_threshold (lane B4 part 3): how much light above the threshold blooms; Emerson found the sun far too bloomy at 0.5 with everything blooming. Lane LOOK2 (2026-10-03, the washed-out fix): agx_white and agx_contrast drive the AgX tonemapper (white is only read by the older tonemappers; AgX's own default white of 16.29 left sunlit ground near 140 of 255), volumetric_ambient_inject is how much sky light the volumetric fog picks up (0.4 before: a milky veil over every distance). Measure with tools/histogram.py.",
